  "notes": [
    {
      "id": "SCOPE-01",
      "kind": "CLARIFICATION",
      "text": "The task owner clarified GPU0-only applies to neural workers. GPU0 AND GPU1 memory/free/utilization sampling is intentional and disclosed so the continuing GPU1 dev workload is visible. The sampled fields contain no power or temperature."
    },
    {
      "id": "MEASUREMENT-01",
      "kind": "LIMITATION",
      "text": "aggregate_fps is 1024/(latest worker finish minus earliest worker start). It includes eight initializations, 1016 tracking steps, image decoding, result-list construction and per-stream final-state hashing. Model construction, imports, warmups and post-timing model-state verification/report serialization are excluded."
    },
    {
      "id": "MEASUREMENT-02",
      "kind": "LIMITATION",
      "text": "end_to_end_seconds/fps cover parent process-spawn to child-join, including per-worker load/warmup and post-timing verification/output. They exclude parent source/input hashing, filesystem prewarm, monitor setup/teardown and final report writing; they are not whole-command latency. load_seconds begins after imports and includes CPU snapshot plus warmup."
    },
    {
      "id": "MEASUREMENT-03",
      "kind": "LIMITATION",
      "text": "cpu_children_seconds uses RUSAGE_CHILDREN. Reaped workers contribute their complete lifetime CPU use, including loading/warmup and final verification, while nvidia-smi subprocesses reaped during the interval also contribute. Do not describe this as inference-only CPU time or divide it by inference wall time to claim inference CPU utilization."
    },
    {
      "id": "MEASUREMENT-04",
      "kind": "LIMITATION",
      "text": "One-second GPU samples observe aggregate device utilization and sampled memory peaks, not exact transient allocation peaks. The memory projection is an empirical admission estimate, not a proof against OOM. The fixed 1024-frame warm-filesystem workload, ordered arms and changing background host load do not establish full-dev/test FPS or a universal optimal worker/thread count."
    },
    {
      "id": "MEASUREMENT-05",
      "kind": "LIMITATION",
      "text": "The two cProfile arms each use the first 128-frame TRAIN stream. They are excluded from throughput selection. Python cumulative timing can include CUDA waits and is not a CUDA kernel profile. Retain repeated N1 results and GPU1 samples when interpreting drift."
    },
    {
      "id": "GATE-01",
      "kind": "RUNTIME_REQUIRED",
      "text": "Per-arm COMPLETE files are written before cross-arm parity is asserted. Accept the benchmark only with the top-level COMPLETE, all required parity flags and the native run_task exit0 receipt. Source PASS and CPU fake parity do not establish actual GPU parity or performance."
    },
    {
      "id": "INPUT-01",
      "kind": "LIMITATION",
      "text": "14 of 26 bound inputs exist locally and all match. 12 remote-only inputs, including model binaries and the full train manifest, were not locally rehashed. Existing migration/training/terminal receipts bind them; main enforces every planned input/source SHA before and after actual execution. This reviewer made no remote query."
    },
    {
      "id": "PROVENANCE-01",
      "kind": "INHERITED_WARNING",
      "text": "The original RankSTOP training launch still has no native terminal exit receipt; its actual training exit code remains unknown. The separately observed cost0 full97 dev native exit0 is valid and must not be substituted for the missing training receipt."
    }
  ],
